              v
       tb277 eth3  00:0d:b9:55:77:0e  10.38.22.33/27
              |
              +--> tools/smtpsrv.py on TCP 11025   (our instrument: STEPs 0, 0b, 1-8)
              +--> the box's own Postfix on TCP 25 (an independent server: STEP 9)

  DUT   : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 @ 115200, S/N A2WQS700B,
          vlan10 "Hardware is VLAN, address is e01a.ead4.7043", IPv4 10.38.22.34/27.
          Single unit, no stack.
  link  : swi_d port1.0.10 <-> tb277 eth3 (copper, vlan10, directly connected /27)
  host  : tb277 eth3, MAC 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e, 10.38.22.33/27 -> swi_d port1.0.10
  tools : tools/smtpsrv.py   -- the SMTP server, on the box, TCP 11025. It can require
                                authentication and can advertise any subset of PLAIN,
                                LOGIN and CRAM-MD5. It writes a timestamped transcript
                                of every line in both directions. The DUT is the client,
                                so this server transcript IS the wire.
          tools/conkey.py    -- sends raw keys to the console. `mail to <addr> subject <s>`
                                is interactive, so the message body and the Ctrl-D that
                                ends it cannot be sent by a prompt-driven tool.
          tools/tb capture + tools/tcpflow.py -- a packet capture on eth3, decoded offline.
