THE CLI SURFACE, read with `?` completion before any command was sent
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The three sub-options are SIBLINGS of the server address, not sub-options of it.
  Each one is its own configuration line.

awplus(config)# mail smtpserver  ?
  A.B.C.D         IPv4 address of SMTP Server
  WORD            Fully Qualified Domain Name of SMTP Server
  X:X::X:X        IPv6 address of SMTP Server
  authentication  Authentication mechanism
  port            SMTP server port
  tls             Use TLS connection to secure sending mail

awplus(config)# mail smtpserver 10.38.22.33  ?
  <cr>                                   <-- the address accepts nothing after it
awplus(config)# mail smtpserver 10.38.22.33 authentication  ?
  % Unrecognized command                 <-- so it is not a sub-option of the address

  The four mechanisms the DUT offers are crammd5, login, oauth2 and plain. For crammd5,
  login and plain the parser then requires `username <USERNAME>` and `password <PASSWORD>`.
  For oauth2 it offers `<cr>`: no username and no password.

