  04:09:48Z S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
  04:09:48Z C: Subject: T33368-A4-crammd5-good   -> 250 queued
  DUT console: ^DSending 20261023040947.11300... ok.
  => STEP 3 PASS: this is the strongest of the three. The server made a fresh random
     challenge and checked HMAC-MD5 of the password over that challenge itself. The DUT
     returned the correct digest. The password never crossed the wire. So the DUT really
     computes the digest from the configured password. It does not replay a stored string.
     STEP 7 closes the proof by showing the digest changes when the password changes.

STEP 4 -- `mail smtpserver authentication oauth2`                                      UNSUPPORTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: the command was sent twice from a state where crammd5 was configured, and once
  more from a state where no mechanism was configured at all.

  From a configured state (crammd5 was in force):
  17:10:52 awplus# configure terminal
  17:10:53 awplus(config)# mail smtpserver authentication oauth2
  17:10:54 awplus(config)# end          <-- no error, no warning, no % line of any kind
  17:10:56 awplus# show mail
             Authentication : crammd5   <-- still crammd5
  awplus# show running-config
             mail smtpserver authentication crammd5 username ckmail password 8 fbq5A0iO...
                                           ^^^^^^^ unchanged
  The next message went out on the wire as:
             04:11:03Z C: AUTH CRAM-MD5  <-- still CRAM-MD5, not oauth2 and not nothing
  Repeated at 17:11:49 with the same command: running-config still reads crammd5.

  From a clean state (after `no mail smtpserver authentication`, nothing configured):
  17:13:03 awplus(config)# mail smtpserver authentication oauth2    <-- accepted again, in silence
  awplus# show running-config -> holds `mail smtpserver 10.38.22.33` and
          `mail smtpserver port 11025` and NO `authentication` line at all
  awplus# show mail           -> no Authentication field, no Username field

  The device then contradicts itself in its own words:
awplus# show mail oauth2 url
  % The smtpserver is not configured for OAUTH2
  <-- read straight after the CLI had accepted the oauth2 command without complaint

  => STEP 4 UNSUPPORTED: oauth2 is only half built on this software version. The CLI token
     exists and the function does not, and the device says so itself. A missing feature is
     UNSUPPORTED, not a failure.
     FINDING, and it is the silence, not the absence. The parser OFFERS oauth2:
     `mail smtpserver authentication ?` lists `oauth2  OAUTH2 authentication`, and
     `mail smtpserver authentication oauth2 ?` offers `<cr>`. So it is a complete, valid
     command, not a truncated one. The device accepts it with no diagnostic. It then has
     no effect on running-config, on `show mail`, or on the wire. The previous mechanism
     stays in force. That has a security cost. An operator who sets oauth2 believes the
     device has moved to token authentication. It has not. It keeps sending the password:
     inside a CRAM-MD5 digest here, and in base64 clear text if the previous setting had
     been `plain`. The operator gets no signal. The device should reject the command with
     a diagnostic instead of accepting it in silence. Reproduced three times.

STEP 5 -- does `port` or `tls` displace `authentication`?                              PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: the three sub-options are separate configuration lines, so each was set while
  the others were already set, and all fields were read back each time. crammd5 was the
  configured mechanism throughout.
awplus(config)# mail smtpserver tls starttls
